            <ArticleTitle>Angina during hemodialysis. Treatment by coronary bypass graft.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>736-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In a 52-year-old man with chronic renal failure, severe angina occured when he was receiving hemodialysis. A double coronary bypass graft was performed, providing complete relief.</AbstractText>
